/* MvOptionCard — large selectable icon-over-label card ("Selecione seu perfil").
 * Spec: DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §6 row 4, §8.5 "Selecione seu perfil".
 * Figma: `Turista Option` / `Guia Option` 109:1035 (Tela 11, both unselected)
 * and 109:4210 (Tela 12, Turista selected) — 174x93, V, gap 12, pad 16,
 * xCENTER, surface fill, r16; unselected 1px outline-variant, selected 2px primary.
 *
 * NOTE: no hex literals anywhere in this file, comments included —
 * TokenDisciplineTests.ComponentUss_HasNoHardcodedColors scans the raw text.
 *
 * GEOMETRY (1 USS px = 1 dp = 1 Figma pt, §1.2)
 *   card    height 93 (authored as a min-height — see the label rule), r16,
 *           padding 16, column, cross-axis centered
 *   icon    32dp slot holding a 24dp glyph (V2 nests a 24x24 icon frame inside a
 *           32x32 box; Material Symbols draw inside their em box, so font-size 24
 *           in a 32dp-tall slot reproduces both numbers)
 *   label   14px, 600 unselected / 700 selected, 12dp below the icon
 *
 * WIDTH IS THE CALLER'S — same rule as MvAlertBar
 *   V2's "174" is one half of the 358dp content column minus the 12dp gap
 *   ((358 - 12) / 2 = 173), and the four frames disagree with themselves about it
 *   (173/173 on Tela 11, 174/172 on Tela 12) — rounding noise from a flex row, not
 *   a property of the card. So the card grows into whatever its row leaves and
 *   shrinks below 173 on a 360dp phone instead of overflowing, the same choice
 *   MvHeroHeader made for its selector pill. A caller wanting a fixed 174 sets it.
 *
 * SELECTED BORDER GROWS INWARD
 *   1px -> 2px would push the content 1dp up and in. The padding drops to 15 on
 *   the selected card so the icon and label do not move — MdChip.uss pulls the
 *   same trick when its selected variant drops its border.
 *
 * LABEL WEIGHT CHANGES WITH SELECTION — and that is from the design
 *   Every V2 frame draws the SELECTED profile label at 700 and the unselected one
 *   at 600 (Tela 3, 5 and 12 all show exactly that pair; Tela 11 has neither
 *   selected and draws both at 600). §8.5 flattens this to "Inter 700 14" — the
 *   frames win, and the weight swap is a second, color-blind selection cue on top
 *   of the border. The card is fixed-width and centers its label, so the extra
 *   stroke width reflows nothing.
 */

.mv-option-card {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    flex-basis: 0;
    /* Let it shrink below its content on a narrow phone rather than overflow. */
    min-width: 0;
    /* A floor, not a fixed height — the label wraps; see the label rule below. */
    min-height: 93px;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 16px;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-large);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface);
    /* V2 paints icon and label in the brand navy — the same ink it uses for every
     * form section label, i.e. the swatch Appendix A.1 maps to `primary`. As ink on
     * a white card that collapses onto `on-surface`, the same collapse A.1 makes for
     * the mid-grey body color; `primary` itself would be an M3 role violation for
     * body text and would go pale blue in the dark theme. Set on the card so the
     * icon and the label move together — including when disabled. */
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface);
    /* Required by the state-layer contract: the layer must follow the corners. */
    overflow: hidden;
}

.mv-option-card:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
}

/* 32dp slot, 24dp glyph. `color` is inherited from the card so a disabled or
 * selected card tints icon and label together. */
.mv-option-card__icon {
    height: 32px;
    font-size: 24px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* label-large metrics (14px / ls 0) at V2's 600 face. */
.mv-option-card__label {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    /* WRAPS, and the card's height is a FLOOR because of it. V2's 93dp fits one
     * line at the authored 174dp width, but the two strings are real words
     * ("Turista" / "Condutor" or longer) and at a larger OS font scale, or on a
     * 360dp phone, one line stops fitting — an ellipsized "Desabilit…" is a worse
     * answer than a second line, and clipping a wrapped line behind the card's
     * `overflow: hidden` would be worse still. Hence `min-height` on the card
     * rather than `height`: a wrapped label grows it, and the sibling card follows
     * because their row stretches. */
    white-space: normal;
    max-width: 100%;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-SemiBold.asset");
}

/* ---- Selected ---- */

.mv-option-card--selected {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
    /* 16 - 1 = 15: compensates the extra border so nothing shifts. */
    padding: 15px;
}

.mv-option-card--selected .mv-option-card__label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-Bold.asset");
}

/* ---- Interaction states ---- */

.mv-option-card .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
}
.mv-option-card--selected .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}

.mv-option-card:hover .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-hover-opacity);
}
.mv-option-card:focus .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-focus-opacity);
}
.mv-option-card:active .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-pressed-opacity);
}

/* ---- Disabled ---- */

.mv-option-card:disabled {
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-container);
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-content);
}
